cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ledger, please cite it as below."
title: "ledger — a privacy-first community archive for queer histories and mutual-aid knowledge"
abstract: >-
  A digital-preservation tool that lets a queer community keep its own records in
  content-addressed, checksummed, replicated storage with consent-based, selective
  disclosure, designed so that holding a record can never out the person who made it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chelsea
    family-names: Kelly-Reif
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/ledger"
url: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/ledger"
# `version` mirrors pyproject.toml, which is the single source of truth for it;
# tools/check_claims.py re-derives this line from there.
# A release date is still deliberately absent: no `git tag` exists for this project
# yet. The version above is now the prepared `0.1.0` rather than a `.dev` string, but
# preparing a release and publishing one are different facts, and only the second one
# has a date. The date that used to sit here, 2026-06-16, was the day an earlier 0.1.0
# candidate was prepared and NOT tagged; publishing it as `date-released` in the file
# citation tooling reads made a rejected candidate look like a shipped release.
# Add `date-released` back in the same commit that cuts the tag, not before, and
# retire the `citation-claims-no-release-date` claim then — docs/RELEASE-0.1.0.md
# carries this as a checklist item.
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - digital-preservation
  - community-archives
  - privacy
  - consent
  - OAIS
  - BagIt
  - PREMIS
  - Dublin-Core
